  {
   "id": "bridge-receiver",
   "title": "Bridge sensor, transmitter and receiver",
   "page": 9,
   "description": "VREF excites a resistor bridge whose low corner returns to IRET. An amplifier powered from VREG with its negative supply on IRET takes the bridge's two midpoints and drives its output straight into IIN. The NPN Q1 carries the loop current from V+ to E, and C1 sits across V+ and IO. At the far end of the two-wire run, VLOOP's positive side feeds the line to V+ and an LDO that powers an ADC; the loop current returns through RLOAD to VLOOP's negative side, which is ground. The ADC reads VLOAD across RLOAD, VLOAD = RLOAD × IO, and IO = 100 × IIN.",
   "parts": [
    {
     "ref": "U1",
     "type": "ic",
     "value": "XTR115/XTR116"
    },
