   "description": "VREF excites a resistor bridge returned to IRET. A front-end amplifier, supplied from VREG with IRET as its ground, takes the bridge midpoints and produces VIN, which drives IIN through RIN = 20 kΩ. For 4 mA to 20 mA out, IIN runs 40 µA to 200 µA, so VIN runs 0.8 V to 4 V. The NPN Q1 carries the loop current, 10 nF sits from V+ to IO, and the loop supply VLOOP and load RL close the two-wire loop. Every current drawn from VREG and VREF comes back into IRET.",
